 "rule": "Anthony's rule (plan step 1.6): a session runs from 18:00 New York the evening before to 17:00 New York on its session date, and a weekend rolls to Monday. From 17:00 a moment is dated the next day; a Saturday or Sunday date rolls to Monday; with the shared calendar, a closed day rolls on as a weekend does.",
 "how_made": "Every expected value was computed with zoneinfo (America/New_York) and session windows, never by the module it proves; each repo's test computes them again the same way. Labels are made up. Every date in the table was chosen by code clear of both fences (Bot-Lab botlab/reserved.py and market-data caretaker/holdout.py), the day before it and the next weekday included; the tests check it again.",
